WEBVTT

00:00:00.598 --> 00:00:01.390
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.638 --> 00:00:06.290
In this lesson, I will show you how to remove a set of gel polish properly,

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:08.990
step by step, so that all the gel comes off,

00:00:09.259 --> 00:00:11.790
and the natural nail of the client stays intact.

00:00:12.219 --> 00:00:14.190
There is only one principle throughout:

00:00:14.459 --> 00:00:16.350
the gel must come off by itself.

00:00:16.619 --> 00:00:20.110
We do not peel, we do not pry, we do not scrape.

00:00:20.619 --> 00:00:23.790
Proper removal takes time, usually about half an hour.

00:00:23.954 --> 00:00:27.870
When you take the booking, allow enough time for it, so you never have to rush.

00:00:28.522 --> 00:00:29.241
Step one:

00:00:29.566 --> 00:00:34.521
wash and sanitize your hands, and the hands of the client, then observe and ask.

00:00:34.945 --> 00:00:37.561
Is it regular gel polish, or builder gel?

00:00:37.978 --> 00:00:39.961
Where was it done, and how long ago?

00:00:40.365 --> 00:00:43.081
Regular gel polish can be soaked off in acetone.

00:00:43.432 --> 00:00:45.161
Hard gel does not dissolve;

00:00:45.349 --> 00:00:49.001
it has to be filed down thin, and I will cover that at the end of the lesson.

00:00:49.427 --> 00:00:51.321
Look at the skin around the nails as well:

00:00:51.561 --> 00:00:55.526
if it is swollen, red, has pus or an open wound, stop,

00:00:55.476 --> 00:00:58.281
and advise the client to see a doctor.

00:00:58.953 --> 00:00:59.733
Step two:

00:00:59.946 --> 00:01:00.853
preparation.

00:01:01.516 --> 00:01:05.813
A 180 grit file and a fine buffer, a new set for every client.

00:01:06.482 --> 00:01:10.773
Cotton pads that do not shed fibers, cut small to the size of the nail.

00:01:11.278 --> 00:01:14.053
Foil cut in advance, or clips for soaking.

00:01:14.562 --> 00:01:17.653
A bottle of acetone, or the gel remover of the brand.

00:01:18.024 --> 00:01:22.613
Wooden sticks, a sterilized pusher, cuticle oil, and gloves.

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:24.533
The room must be ventilated.

00:01:24.706 --> 00:01:29.493
No candles and no flames on the table, because acetone is highly flammable.

00:01:29.802 --> 00:01:31.413
Put on gloves before you start.

00:01:31.581 --> 00:01:34.693
If your gloves get wet with chemicals, change to a new pair.

00:01:35.333 --> 00:01:36.154
Step three:

00:01:36.455 --> 00:01:37.594
break the top coat.

00:01:38.076 --> 00:01:41.034
With one hand, hold the finger of the client firmly.

00:01:41.393 --> 00:01:45.800
Lay the file flat on the nail, and file lightly and evenly all over,

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:47.594
until all the shine is gone.

00:01:48.098 --> 00:01:51.914
When the dust changes to the color of the polish, you are through the top coat.

00:01:52.422 --> 00:01:55.673
Even if the polish on a nail has already lifted at a corner,

00:01:55.623 --> 00:01:57.754
never use that as a place to pry it up.

00:01:58.294 --> 00:02:01.761
Remember the area right next to the cuticle, and both sides.

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:05.761
Do not file the skin, and do not file down to the natural nail.

00:02:06.019 --> 00:02:08.721
Skip this step, and the chemical cannot get in;

00:02:08.902 --> 00:02:11.601
however long you soak, the gel will not soften.

00:02:11.855 --> 00:02:14.001
When you are done, brush the dust away.

00:02:14.255 --> 00:02:15.041
Do not blow.

00:02:15.684 --> 00:02:16.579
Step four:

00:02:16.762 --> 00:02:17.859
protect the skin.

00:02:18.204 --> 00:02:22.179
Apply a little cuticle oil, or cream, to the skin around the nail.

00:02:22.524 --> 00:02:23.539
Only on the skin.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:27.459
Do not let the oil cover the nail plate, because oil blocks the chemical.

00:02:28.051 --> 00:02:28.994
Step five:

00:02:29.155 --> 00:02:29.794
soaking.

00:02:30.274 --> 00:02:34.255
Soak a small piece of cotton with acetone, wet through but not dripping,

00:02:34.205 --> 00:02:36.274
and place it right on the nail plate.

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:40.194
If the cotton is too big, the chemical soaks into the skin as well.

00:02:40.542 --> 00:02:42.354
Just the size of the nail is enough.

00:02:42.783 --> 00:02:45.746
Wrap foil around the fingertip, and squeeze it closed,

00:02:45.696 --> 00:02:47.634
so the chemical does not evaporate.

00:02:48.063 --> 00:02:50.594
Do all five fingers of one hand in turn.

00:02:50.759 --> 00:02:54.434
If you use clips, the clip holds the cotton pressed against the nail.

00:02:54.689 --> 00:02:57.634
After pouring the chemical, close the bottle right away.

00:02:58.260 --> 00:02:59.170
Now we wait.

00:02:59.419 --> 00:03:01.185
Usually ten to fifteen minutes,

00:03:01.135 --> 00:03:04.450
but follow exactly the instructions of the product you use.

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:07.410
While waiting, do not keep opening it to check.

00:03:07.839 --> 00:03:11.490
If the hands of the client are cold, the gel softens more slowly;

00:03:11.759 --> 00:03:13.970
you can put a towel over them to keep them warm.

00:03:14.319 --> 00:03:15.170
A small tip:

00:03:15.512 --> 00:03:18.476
wrap the first hand completely, then the second hand,

00:03:18.426 --> 00:03:20.290
and open them in that same order.

00:03:20.529 --> 00:03:23.250
That way, each hand soaks long enough.

00:03:23.556 --> 00:03:26.610
When the time is up, open one finger at a time.

00:03:26.989 --> 00:03:31.730
Work on each finger as soon as you open it, so the gel has no time to harden again.

00:03:32.416 --> 00:03:33.346
Step six:

00:03:33.527 --> 00:03:34.706
pushing off the gel.

00:03:35.455 --> 00:03:40.121
The gel is ready when it lifts, cracks, and comes away from the nail by itself,

00:03:40.071 --> 00:03:40.706
like this.

00:03:41.202 --> 00:03:46.073
Hold a wooden stick or a pusher at a very low angle, almost flat along the nail,

00:03:46.023 --> 00:03:49.026
and push gently from the cuticle towards the tip.

00:03:49.615 --> 00:03:53.506
Softened gel almost slides off by itself, with no force.

00:03:54.094 --> 00:03:58.386
If you hold the stick upright and press down, you are scraping, not pushing.

00:03:59.033 --> 00:04:02.637
If you have to press hard to get it off, the gel is not soft yet.

00:04:03.037 --> 00:04:03.997
Stop right away.

00:04:04.334 --> 00:04:06.477
Do not scrape, and do not pry.

00:04:06.887 --> 00:04:12.077
Put the cotton back, wrap it again, soak about five more minutes, then continue.

00:04:12.585 --> 00:04:15.277
Forcing it off scrapes away the natural nail as well.

00:04:15.767 --> 00:04:19.037
The nail will be left with white, rough patches, like this.

00:04:19.699 --> 00:04:20.559
Step seven:

00:04:20.827 --> 00:04:21.519
cleaning up.

00:04:22.091 --> 00:04:26.844
If a thin bit of base gel is left, wipe it with cotton soaked in acetone,

00:04:26.794 --> 00:04:29.679
or glide a fine buffer over it very lightly.

00:04:30.016 --> 00:04:31.999
Just glide to smooth the surface;

00:04:32.268 --> 00:04:33.759
do not buff the nail thinner.

00:04:34.181 --> 00:04:37.279
Work through each finger like this, for both hands.

00:04:37.549 --> 00:04:40.251
Then ask the client to wash her hands with soap,

00:04:40.201 --> 00:04:42.239
to remove the chemical and the dust.

00:04:42.868 --> 00:04:43.602
Step eight:

00:04:43.832 --> 00:04:45.122
assess and care.

00:04:45.678 --> 00:04:48.162
Look closely at the natural nails of the client.

00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:51.362
Freshly uncovered nails look a little white and dry;

00:04:51.711 --> 00:04:54.082
that is dehydration, and oil will help.

00:04:54.509 --> 00:04:56.802
If the nails are healthy, you can repaint them.

00:04:57.060 --> 00:05:00.402
In that case, save the cuticle oil for the end of the service.

00:05:00.651 --> 00:05:03.738
If a nail is thin, soft or sore when pressed,

00:05:03.688 --> 00:05:07.922
advise the client to take a break from gel, use oil every day,

00:05:08.066 --> 00:05:10.162
and wear gloves when washing up or cleaning.

00:05:10.496 --> 00:05:13.801
And a nail that is separating from the nail bed, discolored,

00:05:13.751 --> 00:05:16.242
or showing signs of infection is not painted;

00:05:16.509 --> 00:05:18.242
advise the client to see a doctor.

00:05:18.838 --> 00:05:23.684
As for hard gel, the kind that does not dissolve in acetone, do not soak it.

00:05:24.267 --> 00:05:27.332
With a hand file, take the gel down gradually,

00:05:27.282 --> 00:05:30.084
until only a very thin base layer is left.

00:05:30.428 --> 00:05:33.524
Stop there, and do not file into the natural nail.

00:05:33.866 --> 00:05:35.924
This base layer will grow out with the nail.

00:05:36.293 --> 00:05:40.324
An electric file does this faster, but it is only for people who have been trained.

00:05:40.593 --> 00:05:43.044
Filing and drilling make a lot of gel dust:

00:05:43.206 --> 00:05:47.124
wear gloves and a mask, and use a dust extractor if you have one.

00:05:47.686 --> 00:05:49.143
Once the client has gone:

00:05:49.312 --> 00:05:54.023
used foil, cotton, wooden sticks and files go in a bin with a lid.

00:05:54.358 --> 00:05:58.103
Metal pushers and soaking clips go to be washed and disinfected.

00:05:58.410 --> 00:06:00.103
Metal tools are sterilized.

00:06:00.376 --> 00:06:03.703
Close the chemical bottles tightly, and wipe the table clean.

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:04.983
And tell the client:

00:06:05.252 --> 00:06:08.423
next time the gel lifts, do not peel it off at home;

00:06:08.692 --> 00:06:09.863
come back to the salon.

00:06:10.282 --> 00:06:12.903
And now, take the short quiz below the video.
